{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AQgbR8hbxCX65YoW8GhTDe","type":"tool_result","content":"Error: result (246,450 characters) exceeds maximum allowed tokens. Output has been saved to /Users/jim/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-rz-r6wxvr0n15d906k2s0jw8j2h0000gn-T-t008-claude-worker-001-n4hj0go7/535f6348-4431-46d7-8be9-cc4226928f8b/tool-results/mcp-ac-source_read-1792359224145.txt.\nFormat: JSON with schema: {evidence: {id: string, sha256: string}, id: string, operation: string, operation_outcome: {cause: string, core_value: string, evidence: [], limits: [string], predicate: string, source_parent: {...}, value: string}, refusal: null, result: {artifact: null, value: {...}}, schema: string, status: string}\nUse jq to make structured queries (find a value, filter by field).\nREQUIREMENTS FOR SUMMARIZATION/ANALYSIS/REVIEW:\n- You MUST read the content from the file at /Users/jim/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-rz-r6wxvr0n15d906k2s0jw8j2h0000gn-T-t008-claude-worker-001-n4hj0go7/535f6348-4431-46d7-8be9-cc4226928f8b/tool-results/mcp-ac-source_read-1792359224145.txt in sequential chunks until 100% of the content has been read.\n- Note: this file is JSON, so a long value (or the whole file) is a single line. Read's offset/limit cannot split a line, so reading in chunks works only if every line is short. If a shell tool is available, first probe the structure (e.g., jq 'type, length, keys?' /Users/jim/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-rz-r6wxvr0n15d906k2s0jw8j2h0000gn-T-t008-claude-worker-001-n4hj0go7/535f6348-4431-46d7-8be9-cc4226928f8b/tool-results/mcp-ac-source_read-1792359224145.txt), then extract slices with jq or python.\n- If you receive truncation warnings when reading the file, reduce the chunk size until you have read 100% of the content without truncation.\n- Before producing ANY summary or analysis, you MUST explicitly describe what portion of the content you have read. ***If you did not read the entire content