h a full request\\nenvelope. A policy lists core capabilities separately from the operations its\\nprincipals may perform.\\n\\nSetup resolves the operator-selected fresh output to its actual canonical path\\nbefore creating any policy or source binding. `SETUP.json` records those exact\\npaths. Use them for subsequent invocations; registered source/evidence paths\\ncontinue to refuse symlink aliases such as a macOS `/var` alias. No admitted\\npath or source hash is silently replaced.\\n\\nRun the negative example with `requests/denied-preflight.json`: it returns a\\nrefusal and CLI exit 2. Changing the policy without changing the operator's\\nexpected digest also refuses. The setup will not overwrite an existing output\\ndirectory. Keep any partial directory after a setup failure as observed evidence;\\nchoose a fresh output for another attempt.\\n\\nFor a real task, the Product operator supplies an existing Product-located owner\\nbinding and work grant, exact role/packet/return contract, source and method\\nbases, effect territory, evidence surface, registered executor and dependency\\npins. Discover their concrete contracts with `tools.describe` and re-enter the\\n[tenant design](../../design/fd-support.md). Source hashes establish exact bytes;\\nthey do not authenticate whoever wrote a grant. Register no arbitrary caller\\nshell command, argv suffix, environment or endpoint.\\n\\nThe ordinary development path is caller-selected: Executive acquires current\\nsource and prepares a contract; Worker acquires deciding source/proof and\\nreturns its candidate; Reviewer records actual source-derived expectations\\nbefore candidate exposure, then acquires candidate/proof directly. The selected\\nF_P actors and existing owner retain semantic judgment and disposition. Only\\nactual final output from a registered dispatched Attempt can authenticate a\\nreturn through this tool. Fresh contexts, example personas and fixture answers\\nprove no independent semantic result or actor usability.\\n\\nActual actor/provider runs require their separately selected exact executor,\\nconfiguration, context, source/exposure plan and approved work authority. This\\nsetup invokes none. Source-first transport records establish scoped writes,\\nnot that an actor mentally attended to the supplied bytes. Missing delivery or\\nexternal exposure remains unknown.\\n\\n## Optional CLI transport helper\\n\\n`actor_cli.py` is a stdlib adapter for a separately registered Claude or Codex\\nCLI executor. It forwards the exact stdin Context bytes, captures the actual\\nvendor stdout/stderr, and emits the actual final answer bytes. It supplies no\\nprompt, model, grant, default answer, semantic repair or retry. A direct helper\\nrun authenticates no actor. Authentication and the exact Context/activation\\nbinding come from an admitted registered Attempt through the ordinary tool.\\n\\nAn operator first freezes a JSON plan and its raw SHA-256. The closed plan has\\nthese fields; none can be supplied as a public tool argument or argv suffix:\\n\\n| Field | Operator-selected value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `schema`, `id`, `backend` | `a_c.fd-support.actor-cli-plan/1`, a fixed identifier, and `claude` or `codex` |\\n| `executable` | Actual regular-file absolute `path` and lowercase byte `sha256` |\\n| `argv` | Complete fixed argument array, beginning with that executable path |\\n| `dependencies` | Explicit array of regular-file `{path, sha256}` pins, including scripts, loaders and configuration used by the registered call |\\n| `cwd` | Exact existing absolute working directory |\\n| `environment` | Complete selected string map, apart from protected unchanged pass-through below |\\n| `settings` | Exact operator-declared selected settings and known unknowns; declarations never override argv or infer defaults |\\n| `decoder` | One of the three fixed profiles below, matching the backend |\\n| `evidence_directory` | Fresh absolute directory under an existing operator-owned parent |\\n| `limits` | Positive integer `max_input_bytes`, `max_output_bytes`, `timeout_ms`, `termination_grace_ms` |\\n\\nRegister the helper interpreter, helper, core parser, frozen plan, native\\nexecutable and its actual loader/configuration chain under the existing\\nExecutor dependency controls. The helper rechecks plan and listed file pins\\nimmediately before child launch. It rejects symlink path components and starts\\nthe fixed argv without a shell. Pinning a path or configuration file is not a\\nclaim that it covers all host effects or all dynamically loaded dependencies.\\n\\n`HOME`, `home` and `CODEX_HOME` cannot appear in the plan environment. If already\\npresent in the registered helper process, they pass through unchanged and are\\nrecorded separately with that provenance. Absent values stay absent. The\\nhelper reads no credentials or authentication files. Other selected environment\\nvalues are explicit; an operator must not place credential values in the plan\\nor its retained evidence. Existing CLI authentication stays with that CLI.\\n\\nThe selected decoder is part of the frozen plan:\\n\\n- `claude-result-json/1` requires one JSON object: a terminal `type: \\\"result\\\"`,\\n  `subtype: \\\"success\\\"`, `is_error: false`, with nonempty string `result`.\\n- `claude-result-jsonl/1` requires JSON objects on lines and exactly one such\\n  terminal result at the end. Earlier partial events remain raw evidence.\\n- `codex-final-jsonl/1` requires one final `turn.completed` and selects the last\\n  preceding `item.completed` with `item.type: \\\"agent_message\\\"` and string `text`.\\n  Earlier commentary is retained and is never concatenated into the answer.\\n\\nThese are explicit decoder profiles for the documented\\n[Claude JSON/result and streaming formats](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/headless)\\nand [Codex JSONL events](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/non-interactive-mode).\\nThey select final text only; Claude `structured_output` is not an alternative\\nanswer route in these profiles. Multiple turns/results, missing final output,\\nfailed terminal events, malformed JSON and nonzero process exits fail. Later\\nreal-CLI trials must qualify the exact selected executable/profile combination.\\n\\nThe final text must parse through the ordinary integer-only core JSON grammar\\nas an object with `schema: \\\"a_c.fd-support.closed-return/1\\\"`. Its original UTF-8\\nbytes, including whitespace, are forwarded unchanged. Decimal/exponent public\\nnumbers, duplicate keys, nonfinite values, code fences or a missing schema\\nfail; none is repaired. The helper checks only this transport grammar and tag.\\nThe actual return contract, activation identity, proof and semantics remain\\nwith the existing return capture/check and F_P owners.\\n\\nOn each fresh run the helper retains `plan.json`, `context.bin`,\\n`invocation.json`, `vendor.stdout`, `vendor.stderr`, `process.json` and\\n`result.json`, as far as the actual failure permits. A successful decode also\\nretains `final.payload` and `decoded.json`. Vendor usage, settings and costs\\nremain exact raw metadata; decoded evidence supplies source pointers rather\\nthan converting floats or inventing missing usage. No secret values are read\\nfrom the host. The process observation records parent exit, input forwarding,\\npipe EOF, bounds and requested termination. Descendant end, external effects,\\nhost active context, backend retries and semantic outcome remain unknown.\\nAn output bound retains the observed partial chunk and refuses success; it\\nnever truncates a stream into an apparently successful answer.\\n\\nThe existing operator registers a command of this shape only after the plan,\\nauthority, source/exposure path and actual model call have been selected:\\n\\n```sh\\npython3 build_tenants/graphify/examples/fd-support/actor_cli.py --plan \\\"$ac_actor_plan\\\" --plan-sha256 \\\"$ac_actor_plan_sha\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThe helper performs no CLI settings migration. Preserve the selected existing\\nmodel/effort/defaults in the registered argv/configuration and record unresolved\\nhost scope. Installed CLI help and current official references must support\\nthe exact flags. Claude offers explicit tool/MCP selection; `--bare` changes\\nauthentication behavior and is not a substitute for preserving the selected\\nexisting login. No source-supported Codex option confining access to only the\\nselected MCP tools was established for this implementation. A read-only\\nsandbox alone does not establish that confinement. Record that limitation in\\nany proposed Codex packet rather than claiming only-tools isolation.\\n\\nThe helper tests use controlled Python subprocesses with simulated vendor\\nstreams. They establish transport discriminators and never establish actual\\nmodel usability, independence, cost/quality benefit or a Product acceptance.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"eca9c4cbfbd7ad4b712a7d1e8fc73f8cec42b0fb196967b77890833997018f94\",\"selected_sha256\":\"eca9c4cbfbd7ad4b712a7d1e8fc73f8cec42b0fb196967b77890833997018f94\",\"size_bytes\":10729,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/examples/fd-support/README.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"eca9c4cbfbd7ad4b712a7d1e8fc73f8cec42b0fb196967b77890833997018f94\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:faa86f21b899126c109ea18a5cd781fe1b5e74915c2300c05ae5ff91beb24587","sha256":"faa86f21b899126c109ea18a5cd781fe1b5e74915c2300c05ae5ff91beb24587"},"id":"w012-read-setup","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=881e3c7d84bece7916a2c841de73747245c195d0597df221d14c4a2fc507152c]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"# Public support-tool setup\n\n`prepare_readonly.py` creates a fresh, disposable operator configuration for\ndiscovery and exact source acquisition. It uses the ordinary public CLI/MCP,\nthe real policy validator and the shipped method profile. It creates three\nexample principals with the same nine read/query permissions. They are not\nactual F_P actors or independent assessors.\n\nThe configuration has **no work grants or executors**. Its required admission\nbinding contains a visibly unqualified implementation placeholder. It grants\nno Product work and cannot admit preflight, dispatch or authoritative writing.\nThe current Product owner binding is a separate authority surface; this example\ndoes not ratify it. A trusted operator must select and verify real authority\nbefore preparing a real task policy.\n\nFrom `a_c/`, with Python 3.11 or later:\n\n```sh\nac_example_parent=\"$(python3 -c 'import pathlib,tempfile; print(pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp()).resolve())')\"\npython3 build_tenants/graphify/examples/fd-support/prepare_readonly.py --out \"$ac_example_parent/demo\"\nac_example_sha=\"$(python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))[\"policy_sha256\"])' \"$ac_example_parent/demo/SETUP.json\")\"\n\npython3 build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy \"$ac_example_parent/demo/policy.json\" --policy-sha256 \"$ac_example_sha\" --principal executive call --request \"$ac_example_parent/demo/requests/describe.json\"\npython3 build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy \"$ac_example_parent/demo/policy.json\" --policy-sha256 \"$ac_example_sha\" --principal worker call --request \"$ac_example_parent/demo/requests/read-product.json\"\npython3 build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy \"$ac_example_parent/demo/policy.json\" --policy-sha256 \"$ac_example_sha\" --principal reviewer mcp < \"$ac_example_parent/demo/mcp-session.jsonl\"\n```\n\nThe setup output supplies the exact policy byte digest. `source.read` returns\nactual Product Definition content, its parent hash and acquisition route;\n`workspace.observe` observes the named current file. The MCP example initializes,\nlists the same operation contracts and acquires source through a full request\nenvelope. A policy lists core capabilities separately from the operations its\nprincipals may perform.\n\nSetup resolves the operator-selected fresh output to its actual canonical path\nbefore creating any policy or source binding. `SETUP.json` records those exact\npaths. Use them for subsequent invocations; registered source/evidence paths\ncontinue to refuse symlink aliases such as a macOS `/var` alias. No admitted\npath or source hash is silently replaced.\n\nRun the negative example with `requests/denied-preflight.json`: it returns a\nrefusal and CLI exit 2. Changing the policy without changing the operator's\nexpected digest also refuses. The setup will not overwrite an existing output\ndirectory. Keep any partial directory after a setup failure as observed evidence;\nchoose a fresh output for another attempt.\n\nFor a real task, the Product operator supplies an existing Product-located owner\nbinding and work grant, exact role/packet/return contract, source and method\nbases, effect territory, evidence surface, registered executor and dependency\npins. Discover their concrete contracts with `tools.describe` and re-enter the\n[tenant design](../../design/fd-support.md). Source hashes establish exact bytes;\nthey do not authenticate whoever wrote a grant. Register no arbitrary caller\nshell command, argv suffix, environment or endpoint.\n\nThe ordinary development path is caller-selected: Executive acquires current\nsource and prepares a contract; Worker acquires deciding source/proof and\nreturns its candidate; Reviewer records actual source-derived expectations\nbefore candidate exposure, then acquires candidate/proof directly. The selected\nF_P actors and existing owner retain semantic judgment and disposition. Only\nactual final output from a registered dispatched Attempt can authenticate a\nreturn through this tool. Fresh contexts, example personas and fixture answers\nprove no independent semantic result or actor usability.\n\nActual actor/provider runs require their separately selected exact executor,\nconfiguration, context, source/exposure plan and approved work authority. This\nsetup invokes none. Source-first transport records establish scoped writes,\nnot that an actor mentally attended to the supplied bytes. Missing delivery or\nexternal exposure remains unknown.\n\n## Optional CLI transport helper\n\n`actor_cli.py` is a stdlib adapter for a separately registered Claude or Codex\nCLI executor. It forwards the exact stdin Context bytes, captures the actual\nvendor stdout/stderr, and emits the actual final answer bytes. It supplies no\nprompt, model, grant, default answer, semantic repair or retry. A direct helper\nrun authenticates no actor. Authentication and the exact Context/activation\nbinding come from an admitted registered Attempt through the ordinary tool.\n\nAn operator first freezes a JSON plan and its raw SHA-256. The closed plan has\nthese fields; none can be supplied as a public tool argument or argv suffix:\n\n| Field | Operator-selected value |\n| --- | --- |\n| `schema`, `id`, `backend` | `a_c.fd-support.actor-cli-plan/1`, a fixed identifier, and `claude` or `codex` |\n| `executable` | Actual regular-file absolute `path` and lowercase byte `sha256` |\n| `argv` | Complete fixed argument array, beginning with that executable path |\n| `dependencies` | Explicit array of regular-file `{path, sha256}` pins, including scripts, loaders and configuration used by the registered call |\n| `cwd` | Exact existing absolute working directory |\n| `environment` | Complete selected string map, apart from protected unchanged pass-through below |\n| `settings` | Exact operator-declared selected settings and known unknowns; declarations never override argv or infer defaults |\n| `decoder` | One of the three fixed profiles below, matching the backend |\n| `evidence_directory` | Fresh absolute directory under an existing operator-owned parent |\n| `limits` | Positive integer `max_input_bytes`, `max_output_bytes`, `timeout_ms`, `termination_grace_ms` |\n\nRegister the helper interpreter, helper, core parser, frozen plan, native\nexecutable and its actual loader/configuration chain under the existing\nExecutor dependency controls. The helper rechecks plan and listed file pins\nimmediately before child launch. It rejects symlink path components and starts\nthe fixed argv without a shell. Pinning a path or configuration file is not a\nclaim that it covers all host effects or all dynamically loaded dependencies.\n\n`HOME`, `home` and `CODEX_HOME` cannot appear in the plan environment. If already\npresent in the registered helper process, they pass through unchanged and are\nrecorded separately with that provenance. Absent values stay absent. The\nhelper reads no credentials or authentication files. Other selected environment\nvalues are explicit; an operator must not place credential values in the plan\nor its retained evidence. Existing CLI authentication stays with that CLI.\n\nThe selected decoder is part of the frozen plan:\n\n- `claude-result-json/1` requires one JSON object: a terminal `type: \"result\"`,\n  `subtype: \"success\"`, `is_error: false`, with nonempty string `result`.\n- `claude-result-jsonl/1` requires JSON objects on lines and exactly one such\n  terminal result at the end. Earlier partial events remain raw evidence.\n- `codex-final-jsonl/1` requires one final `turn.completed` and selects the last\n  preceding `item.completed` with `item.type: \"agent_message\"` and string `text`.\n  Earlier commentary is retained and is never concatenated into the answer.\n\nThese are explicit decoder profiles for the documented\n[Claude JSON/result and streaming formats](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/headless)\nand [Codex JSONL events](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/non-interactive-mode).\nThey select final text only; Claude `structured_output` is not an alternative\nanswer route in these profiles. Multiple turns/results, missing final output,\nfailed terminal events, malformed JSON and nonzero process exits fail. Later\nreal-CLI trials must qualify the exact selected executable/profile combination.\n\nThe final text must parse through the ordinary integer-only core JSON grammar\nas an object with `schema: \"a_c.fd-support.closed-return/1\"`. Its original UTF-8\nbytes, including whitespace, are forwarded unchanged. Decimal/exponent public\nnumbers, duplicate keys, nonfinite values, code fences or a missing schema\nfail; none is repaired. The helper checks only this transport grammar and tag.\nThe actual return contract, activation identity, proof and semantics remain\nwith the existing return capture/check and F_P owners.\n\nOn each fresh run the helper retains `plan.json`, `context.bin`,\n`invocation.json`, `vendor.stdout`, `vendor.stderr`, `process.json` and\n`result.json`, as far as the actual failure permits. A successful decode also\nretains `final.payload` and `decoded.json`. Vendor usage, settings and costs\nremain exact raw metadata; decoded evidence supplies source pointers rather\nthan converting floats or inventing missing usage. No secret values are read\nfrom the host. The process observation records parent exit, input forwarding,\npipe EOF, bounds and requested termination. Descendant end, external effects,\nhost active context, backend retries and semantic outcome remain unknown.\nAn output bound retains the observed partial chunk and refuses success; it\nnever truncates a stream into an apparently successful answer.\n\nThe existing operator registers a command of this shape only after the plan,\nauthority, source/exposure path and actual model call have been selected:\n\n```sh\npython3 build_tenants/graphify/examples/fd-support/actor_cli.py --plan \"$ac_actor_plan\" --plan-sha256 \"$ac_actor_plan_sha\"\n```\n\nThe helper performs no CLI settings migration. Preserve the selected existing\nmodel/effort/defaults in the registered argv/configuration and record unresolved\nhost scope. Installed CLI help and current official references must support\nthe exact flags. Claude offers explicit tool/MCP selection; `--bare` changes\nauthentication behavior and is not a substitute for preserving the selected\nexisting login. No source-supported Codex option confining access to only the\nselected MCP tools was established for this implementation. A read-only\nsandbox alone does not establish that confinement. Record that limitation in\nany proposed Codex packet rather than claiming only-tools isolation.\n\nThe helper tests use controlled Python subprocesses with simulated vendor\nstreams. They establish transport discriminators and never establish actual\nmodel usability, independence, cost/quality benefit or a Product acceptance.\n","coordinates":null,"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"eca9c4cbfbd7ad4b712a7d1e8fc73f8cec42b0fb196967b77890833997018f94","selected_sha256":"eca9c4cbfbd7ad4b712a7d1e8fc73f8cec42b0fb196967b77890833997018f94","size_bytes":10729,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/examples/fd-support/README.md","root":"product","selector":null,"sha256":"eca9c4cbfbd7ad4b712a7d1e8fc73f8cec42b0fb196967b77890833997018f94"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XWA1xYcCeqduZwjNxue6a1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgARJBJXCdnMqxGnap5iB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01849CXFJcY8KTHUvkyyRQgV","name":"mcp__ac__source_read","input":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"w013-read-how-1-120","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[1,120]},"sha256":"faefdf2432759859780d962ca1028f44f7ebca9a5f6a11c324c27ddc258d521f"},"encoding":"utf8"}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7076,"cache_read_input_tokens":214991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7076},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"535f6348-4431-46d7-8be9-cc4226928f8b","uuid":"f7510036-a156-44b5-a7c9-5c4e96142606","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:33:59.644Z","request_id":"req_011CgARJB1QmtnF35rhiNg9E","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01849CXFJcY8KTHUvkyyRQgV":{"schema":"a_c.fd-support.request/1","id":"w013-read-how-1-120","operation":"source.read","arguments":{"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[1,120]},"sha256":"faefdf2432759859780d962ca1028f44f7ebca9a5f6a11c324c27ddc258d521f"},"encoding":"utf8"}}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01849CXFJcY8KTHUvkyyRQgV","display_name":"Source Read","server_display_name":"a_c.graphify.fd-support","tool_name":"source.read"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01849CXFJcY8KTHUvkyyRQgV","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:29512bc2d6995e00f037b4d92012767e4f1ab42ece9bfb420e7317961f5258f5\",\"sha256\":\"29512bc2d6995e00f037b4d92012767e4f1ab42ece9bfb420e7317961f5258f5\"},\"id\":\"w013-read-how-1-120\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=8071d9f556d879c801f8e5c9e7bf0ce647ad7037973505eef5000a4807bb3d71]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Deterministic support for F_P development actors\\n\\nStatus: **provisional HOW, reconciliation-008 for T-008**. This is tenant HOW for\\n[REQ-AC-FD-001..013](../../../specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md)\\nand the [qualification obligations](../../../specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md).\\nThis document specifies the selected contract; separate closed module returns\\nrecord provisional construction evidence. Integrated qualification, actual F_P\\nassessment, semantic acceptance and benefit remain pending. The unchanged codec\\nand source-generation designs retain their existing checked scopes.\\n\\n## Boundary and method binding\\n\\nThe Product is `urn:stdo:product-definition:a-c-implementations`; Graphify is\\nits existing registered tenant. The increment adds tools to that tenant, not\\nan Executive, scheduler, independent Product, graph-owned workflow, work ledger\\nor method. F_P actors select work, frames, material relations, meaning,\\nassurance claims and already-authorized actions. Named operations acquire,\\nrender, dispatch, retain and record. `F_D[v]` checks evaluate only declared\\nsupported predicates. An executor invoking F_P does not make its answer F_D.\\n\\n[T-008](../../../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-008-fd-tenant-implementation.md)\\nrecords the owner's instruction, exact design activation and external bootstrap\\nadmission. The installed construction constitution stays STDO v2.5.1-rc.2,\\nmanifest `3d860ff4c1746f06ac25295a9e205cffb8e7725869615ac77cf2304b70ff2782`.\\nThe owner selects Claude RC9 for this bounded work's execution, including its\\nExecutive and software-design profiles. This does not rewrite the installed\\nconstitution or assert a published/accepted V3 install.\\n\\nThe [RC9 binding](fd-method-claude-rc9.json) pins source commit\\n`c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3`, custody\\n`3a2097137c3588ba44b98e3ea801ac7f2be1daf0`, standards tree\\n`98de394b352179c25dfa63b0b59a9b6bdd43632d` and exact deciding members. The\\nsame profile is the first finite consumer contract supported by the toolset.\\nThe source-owner map from T-007 remains the prior common-candidate derivation,\\nnot a substituted execution basis. Exact model subjects remain a third basis\\nrole. Runtime imports no V3 code, native compiler, sibling Product, study MCP\\nor generated study model. Method content is supplied through verified source\\nreferences; its source repository need not be mutable or colocated.\\n\\n### Deciding owners and translation scope\\n\\n| Tool relation | Exact RC9 deciding owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Activation carrier and source/identity relations | REFERENCE_FRAME §11 and RF-005/006/012/013/014 |\\n| Contract admission, intake, context/fit, actor duties, effects and recovery | ACTIVATION §§1–3, 5 and 7; TICKETS §5 |\\n| Result predicates, original domain outcomes, gaps, conjunction and reuse | FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Conjunction of results, Change impact and evidence reuse |\\n| Evidence versus semantic law, source-first expectations and independence | EVALUATION §§1–4; ASSURANCE §§3, 10, 13–16 |\\n| Selected role additions, no Executive mutation and event-driven attention | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§6, 8–10, 12, 17 and 19 |\\n| Work/evidence ownership and recorded decisions | TICKETS §7; PRODUCT_DEFINITION §8 |\\n| This source-to-module gate | DESIGN_MODULE §5 Decision-complete symbolic design and §7 three-view gate |\\n\\nThese routes retain source conditions and exclusions. A profile describes a\\nfinite serialization/check binding; it supplies no new method rule. An unknown\\ncut, optional-profile selection, vocabulary, predicate primitive, translation\\nor executor contract refuses specifically. A matching label or hash establishes\\nneither applicability nor authority. No arbitrary cross-method join is supported.\\n\\n## Operating model and trust boundary\\n\\nA trusted local Product operator starts the CLI/server with an exact policy\\nfile, its expected SHA-256 and one fixed principal identity. The operator\\nselects the Product, source roots/repositories, method profile, owner records,\\nexisting work grants, roles, predicate/operator definitions, executors and\\nprotected evidence root. The API caller is untrusted with respect to these\\nchoices. A request cannot create or replace policy, change its principal,\\nregister an executor, grant territory or declare itself owner. Policy bytes\\nare acquired and checked again before effects. Their digest checks continuity;\\nit does not authenticate whoever wrote them. Authority rests on the trusted\\noperator's separately established Product/owner binding.\\n\\nThe supported deployment is a cooperative local development account: the\\noperator and registered executor programs are trusted to honor their declared\\noperation contracts. Requests, workspace content and F_P output are untrusted\\ninput to the tool. Same-account actors able to rewrite protected policy,\\nexecutables or retained evidence behind the server are outside this boundary;\\nthe tool provides no OS credential isolation, signing or adversarial concurrent\\nfilesystem sandbox. It still detects ordinary dirty state, dependency drift,\\nconflicting tool writes, missing evidence and incorrect request boundaries.\\nNo internal path is trusted merely because it is internal.\\n\\nA registered process is **not OS-confined**. Preflight and dispatch enforce\\nits exact invocation, input and configuration, check its registered dependency\\npreimages, and observe declared effect surfaces. They do not prove that an\\narbitrary child cannot write elsewhere or create descendants. An executor's\\nqualified contract must honestly declare its tools, local-effect behavior,\\ndependency population, termination observations and unobserved host conditions.\\nUnsupported enforcement requirements refuse; no `sandboxed` guarantee appears.\\n\\nPolicy/source roots and the protected evidence root cannot be in any permitted\\nWriter territory. All API-relative paths reject absolute paths, `..`, empty or\\nambiguous components and symlink components, including a symlink leaf; regular\\nfile opens use non-following checks. Immutable Git acquisition resolves an\\nexact full object/revision and member, checks regular-blob mode and hash, then\\nreads blob bytes without checkout, hooks, filters or a moving branch. Product\\nread roots may exceed write territory only where explicitly configured. A\\nmissing or inaccessible root is a gap, never permission to search elsewhere.\\n\\n## Ontology and invariants\\n\\nThe irreducible domain carriers are the selected policy/binding, exact acquired\\ncontent/observations, activated context, one execution attempt, original return\\nand downstream operation evidence. Files, CLI messages and MCP results are\\nrepresentations of those carriers. No separate mutable task object is needed.\\n\\n| Carrier | Identity, ownership and relationship |\\n|---|---|\\n| `OwnerPolicy` | One exact operator-selected id/digest per Runtime, binding one Product definition id/digest and fixed principal. Contains existing grants and approved operation/executor/predicate references. External authority, never public-tool output. |\\n| `MethodBinding` | One exact registered profile id/digest and method cut plus member hashes. References owners; maps their packet/result contracts to tenant serialization. |\\n| `SourceRef` | One engine, registered root/repository, exact relative path/object and whole-content SHA-256. One optional selector narrows acquisition, never changes parent identity. |\\n| `Observation` | One named acquisition scope/time, enumerated path population, existence/mode/byte hashes and relevant configuration/dependency preconditions. Dirty/untracked bytes participate. |\\n| `ModelRef` | One exact raw input digest, model id/digest, codec/profile and subject basis; source grounding is separately supplied. Model and carrier identities stay distinct. |\\n| `Context` | One caller-selected method packet plus actual record/source payloads, late-acquisition manifest, projection boundaries, rendered stdin bytes and scoped fit evidence. |\\n| `Preflight` | One exact activation/context/grant/executor/result-surface tuple, policy and source preimages, finite admission findings and receipt. It does not admit its cited outcome. |\\n| `Attempt` | One protected identity/reservation, exact invocation/payload/settings, ordered retained observations, stdout/stderr and named result surface. May have predecessor attempt; never an inferred continuation. |\\n| `ClosedReturn` | One original raw payload and producer/activation/subject/basis/consumer bindings, original predicates/domain values, provenance, residuals and invalidators. Checks do not rewrite it. |\\n| `OperationEvidence` | One immutable request/response/content manifest and hash-linked observations. Reconstructable downstream evidence, not a work-state authority. |\\n| `ExistingCarrier` | An externally owned work/evidence source. Projection does not own its state. Only a named, separately granted Writer operation changes it. |\\n\\nCross-carrier invariants:\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,120]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"faefdf2432759859780d962ca1028f44f7ebca9a5f6a11c324c27ddc258d521f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"f8a3bd750e9bae0451bd619c6f6ef7bc70005a2f99377a4b58f872cdd16a69ce\",\"size_bytes\":8928,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,120]},\"sha256\":\"faefdf2432759859780d962ca1028f44f7ebca9a5f6a11c324c27ddc258d521f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"535f6348-4431-46d7-8be9-cc4226928f8b","uuid":"dd73bb2f-d2a4-4b7c-94f5-56d576465ea6","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:33:59.654Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:29512bc2d6995e00f037b4d92012767e4f1ab42ece9bfb420e7317961f5258f5\",\"sha256\":\"29512bc2d6995e00f037b4d92012767e4f1ab42ece9bfb420e7317961f5258f5\"},\"id\":\"w013-read-how-1-120\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=8071d9f556d879c801f8e5c9e7bf0ce647ad7037973505eef5000a4807bb3d71]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Deterministic support for F_P development actors\\n\\nStatus: **provisional HOW, reconciliation-008 for T-008**. This is tenant HOW for\\n[REQ-AC-FD-001..013](../../../specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md)\\nand the [qualification obligations](../../../specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md).\\nThis document specifies the selected contract; separate closed module returns\\nrecord provisional construction evidence. Integrated qualification, actual F_P\\nassessment, semantic acceptance and benefit remain pending. The unchanged codec\\nand source-generation designs retain their existing checked scopes.\\n\\n## Boundary and method binding\\n\\nThe Product is `urn:stdo:product-definition:a-c-implementations`; Graphify is\\nits existing registered tenant. The increment adds tools to that tenant, not\\nan Executive, scheduler, independent Product, graph-owned workflow, work ledger\\nor method. F_P actors select work, frames, material relations, meaning,\\nassurance claims and already-authorized actions. Named operations acquire,\\nrender, dispatch, retain and record. `F_D[v]` checks evaluate only declared\\nsupported predicates. An executor invoking F_P does not make its answer F_D.\\n\\n[T-008](../../../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-008-fd-tenant-implementation.md)\\nrecords the owner's instruction, exact design activation and external bootstrap\\nadmission. The installed construction constitution stays STDO v2.5.1-rc.2,\\nmanifest `3d860ff4c1746f06ac25295a9e205cffb8e7725869615ac77cf2304b70ff2782`.\\nThe owner selects Claude RC9 for this bounded work's execution, including its\\nExecutive and software-design profiles. This does not rewrite the installed\\nconstitution or assert a published/accepted V3 install.\\n\\nThe [RC9 binding](fd-method-claude-rc9.json) pins source commit\\n`c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3`, custody\\n`3a2097137c3588ba44b98e3ea801ac7f2be1daf0`, standards tree\\n`98de394b352179c25dfa63b0b59a9b6bdd43632d` and exact deciding members. The\\nsame profile is the first finite consumer contract supported by the toolset.\\nThe source-owner map from T-007 remains the prior common-candidate derivation,\\nnot a substituted execution basis. Exact model subjects remain a third basis\\nrole. Runtime imports no V3 code, native compiler, sibling Product, study MCP\\nor generated study model. Method content is supplied through verified source\\nreferences; its source repository need not be mutable or colocated.\\n\\n### Deciding owners and translation scope\\n\\n| Tool relation | Exact RC9 deciding owner |\\n|---|---|\\n| Activation carrier and source/identity relations | REFERENCE_FRAME §11 and RF-005/006/012/013/014 |\\n| Contract admission, intake, context/fit, actor duties, effects and recovery | ACTIVATION §§1–3, 5 and 7; TICKETS §5 |\\n| Result predicates, original domain outcomes, gaps, conjunction and reuse | FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Conjunction of results, Change impact and evidence reuse |\\n| Evidence versus semantic law, source-first expectations and independence | EVALUATION §§1–4; ASSURANCE §§3, 10, 13–16 |\\n| Selected role additions, no Executive mutation and event-driven attention | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§6, 8–10, 12, 17 and 19 |\\n| Work/evidence ownership and recorded decisions | TICKETS §7; PRODUCT_DEFINITION §8 |\\n| This source-to-module gate | DESIGN_MODULE §5 Decision-complete symbolic design and §7 three-view gate |\\n\\nThese routes retain source conditions and exclusions. A profile describes a\\nfinite serialization/check binding; it supplies no new method rule. An unknown\\ncut, optional-profile selection, vocabulary, predicate primitive, translation\\nor executor contract refuses specifically. A matching label or hash establishes\\nneither applicability nor authority. No arbitrary cross-method join is supported.\\n\\n## Operating model and trust boundary\\n\\nA trusted local Product operator starts the CLI/server with an exact policy\\nfile, its expected SHA-256 and one fixed principal identity. The operator\\nselects the Product, source roots/repositories, method profile, owner records,\\nexisting work grants, roles, predicate/operator definitions, executors and\\nprotected evidence root. The API caller is untrusted with respect to these\\nchoices. A request cannot create or replace policy, change its principal,\\nregister an executor, grant territory or declare itself owner. Policy bytes\\nare acquired and checked again before effects. Their digest checks continuity;\\nit does not authenticate whoever wrote them. Authority rests on the trusted\\noperator's separately established Product/owner binding.\\n\\nThe supported deployment is a cooperative local development account: the\\noperator and registered executor programs are trusted to honor their declared\\noperation contracts. Requests, workspace content and F_P output are untrusted\\ninput to the tool. Same-account actors able to rewrite protected policy,\\nexecutables or retained evidence behind the server are outside this boundary;\\nthe tool provides no OS credential isolation, signing or adversarial concurrent\\nfilesystem sandbox. It still detects ordinary dirty state, dependency drift,\\nconflicting tool writes, missing evidence and incorrect request boundaries.\\nNo internal path is trusted merely because it is internal.\\n\\nA registered process is **not OS-confined**. Preflight and dispatch enforce\\nits exact invocation, input and configuration, check its registered dependency\\npreimages, and observe declared effect surfaces. They do not prove that an\\narbitrary child cannot write elsewhere or create descendants. An executor's\\nqualified contract must honestly declare its tools, local-effect behavior,\\ndependency population, termination observations and unobserved host conditions.\\nUnsupported enforcement requirements refuse; no `sandboxed` guarantee appears.\\n\\nPolicy/source roots and the protected evidence root cannot be in any permitted\\nWriter territory. All API-relative paths reject absolute paths, `..`, empty or\\nambiguous components and symlink components, including a symlink leaf; regular\\nfile opens use non-following checks. Immutable Git acquisition resolves an\\nexact full object/revision and member, checks regular-blob mode and hash, then\\nreads blob bytes without checkout, hooks, filters or a moving branch. Product\\nread roots may exceed write territory only where explicitly configured. A\\nmissing or inaccessible root is a gap, never permission to search elsewhere.\\n\\n## Ontology and invariants\\n\\nThe irreducible domain carriers are the selected policy/binding, exact acquired\\ncontent/observations, activated context, one execution attempt, original return\\nand downstream operation evidence. Files, CLI messages and MCP results are\\nrepresentations of those carriers. No separate mutable task object is needed.\\n\\n| Carrier | Identity, ownership and relationship |\\n|---|---|\\n| `OwnerPolicy` | One exact operator-selected id/digest per Runtime, binding one Product definition id/digest and fixed principal. Contains existing grants and approved operation/executor/predicate references. External authority, never public-tool output. |\\n| `MethodBinding` | One exact registered profile id/digest and method cut plus member hashes. References owners; maps their packet/result contracts to tenant serialization. |\\n| `SourceRef` | One engine, registered root/repository, exact relative path/object and whole-content SHA-256. One optional selector narrows acquisition, never changes parent identity. |\\n| `Observation` | One named acquisition scope/time, enumerated path population, existence/mode/byte hashes and relevant configuration/dependency preconditions. Dirty/untracked bytes participate. |\\n| `ModelRef` | One exact raw input digest, model id/digest, codec/profile and subject basis; source grounding is separately supplied. Model and carrier identities stay distinct. |\\n| `Context` | One caller-selected method packet plus actual record/source payloads, late-acquisition manifest, projection boundaries, rendered stdin bytes and scoped fit evidence. |\\n| `Preflight` | One exact activation/context/grant/executor/result-surface tuple, policy and source preimages, finite admission findings and receipt. It does not admit its cited outcome. |\\n| `Attempt` | One protected identity/reservation, exact invocation/payload/settings, ordered retained observations, stdout/stderr and named result surface. May have predecessor attempt; never an inferred continuation. |\\n| `ClosedReturn` | One original raw payload and producer/activation/subject/basis/consumer bindings, original predicates/domain values, provenance, residuals and invalidators. Checks do not rewrite it. |\\n| `OperationEvidence` | One immutable request/response/content manifest and hash-linked observations. Reconstructable downstream evidence, not a work-state authority. |\\n| `ExistingCarrier` | An externally owned work/evidence source. Projection does not own its state. Only a named, separately granted Writer operation changes it. |\\n\\nCross-carrier invariants:\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,120]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"faefdf2432759859780d962ca1028f44f7ebca9a5f6a11c324c27ddc258d521f\",\"selected_sha256\":\"f8a3bd750e9bae0451bd619c6f6ef7bc70005a2f99377a4b58f872cdd16a69ce\",\"size_bytes\":8928,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,120]},\"sha256\":\"faefdf2432759859780d962ca1028f44f7ebca9a5f6a11c324c27ddc258d521f\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}","structuredContent":{"evidence":{"id":"sha256:29512bc2d6995e00f037b4d92012767e4f1ab42ece9bfb420e7317961f5258f5","sha256":"29512bc2d6995e00f037b4d92012767e4f1ab42ece9bfb420e7317961f5258f5"},"id":"w013-read-how-1-120","operation":"source.read","operation_outcome":{"cause":"declared output available","core_value":"satisfied","evidence":[],"limits":["output availability only; no semantic acceptance"],"predicate":"B(source.read)[request_sha256=8071d9f556d879c801f8e5c9e7bf0ce647ad7037973505eef5000a4807bb3d71]: declared output availability","source_parent":{"clause":"results","member":"FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"fd2d895f90eb39bda0950c1c7ff02057ef5d8ae73fcbc5b3203f7e99081d6e3f"},"value":"returned"},"refusal":null,"result":{"artifact":null,"value":{"acquisition":{},"content":"# Deterministic support for F_P development actors\n\nStatus: **provisional HOW, reconciliation-008 for T-008**. This is tenant HOW for\n[REQ-AC-FD-001..013](../../../specification/requirements/fd-support-tools.md)\nand the [qualification obligations](../../../specification/requirements/fd-support-verification.md).\nThis document specifies the selected contract; separate closed module returns\nrecord provisional construction evidence. Integrated qualification, actual F_P\nassessment, semantic acceptance and benefit remain pending. The unchanged codec\nand source-generation designs retain their existing checked scopes.\n\n## Boundary and method binding\n\nThe Product is `urn:stdo:product-definition:a-c-implementations`; Graphify is\nits existing registered tenant. The increment adds tools to that tenant, not\nan Executive, scheduler, independent Product, graph-owned workflow, work ledger\nor method. F_P actors select work, frames, material relations, meaning,\nassurance claims and already-authorized actions. Named operations acquire,\nrender, dispatch, retain and record. `F_D[v]` checks evaluate only declared\nsupported predicates. An executor invoking F_P does not make its answer F_D.\n\n[T-008](../../../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-008-fd-tenant-implementation.md)\nrecords the owner's instruction, exact design activation and external bootstrap\nadmission. The installed construction constitution stays STDO v2.5.1-rc.2,\nmanifest `3d860ff4c1746f06ac25295a9e205cffb8e7725869615ac77cf2304b70ff2782`.\nThe owner selects Claude RC9 for this bounded work's execution, including its\nExecutive and software-design profiles. This does not rewrite the installed\nconstitution or assert a published/accepted V3 install.\n\nThe [RC9 binding](fd-method-claude-rc9.json) pins source commit\n`c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3`, custody\n`3a2097137c3588ba44b98e3ea801ac7f2be1daf0`, standards tree\n`98de394b352179c25dfa63b0b59a9b6bdd43632d` and exact deciding members. The\nsame profile is the first finite consumer contract supported by the toolset.\nThe source-owner map from T-007 remains the prior common-candidate derivation,\nnot a substituted execution basis. Exact model subjects remain a third basis\nrole. Runtime imports no V3 code, native compiler, sibling Product, study MCP\nor generated study model. Method content is supplied through verified source\nreferences; its source repository need not be mutable or colocated.\n\n### Deciding owners and translation scope\n\n| Tool relation | Exact RC9 deciding owner |\n|---|---|\n| Activation carrier and source/identity relations | REFERENCE_FRAME §11 and RF-005/006/012/013/014 |\n| Contract admission, intake, context/fit, actor duties, effects and recovery | ACTIVATION §§1–3, 5 and 7; TICKETS §5 |\n| Result predicates, original domain outcomes, gaps, conjunction and reuse | FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Conjunction of results, Change impact and evidence reuse |\n| Evidence versus semantic law, source-first expectations and independence | EVALUATION §§1–4; ASSURANCE §§3, 10, 13–16 |\n| Selected role additions, no Executive mutation and event-driven attention | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§6, 8–10, 12, 17 and 19 |\n| Work/evidence ownership and recorded decisions | TICKETS §7; PRODUCT_DEFINITION §8 |\n| This source-to-module gate | DESIGN_MODULE §5 Decision-complete symbolic design and §7 three-view gate |\n\nThese routes retain source conditions and exclusions. A profile describes a\nfinite serialization/check binding; it supplies no new method rule. An unknown\ncut, optional-profile selection, vocabulary, predicate primitive, translation\nor executor contract refuses specifically. A matching label or hash establishes\nneither applicability nor authority. No arbitrary cross-method join is supported.\n\n## Operating model and trust boundary\n\nA trusted local Product operator starts the CLI/server with an exact policy\nfile, its expected SHA-256 and one fixed principal identity. The operator\nselects the Product, source roots/repositories, method profile, owner records,\nexisting work grants, roles, predicate/operator definitions, executors and\nprotected evidence root. The API caller is untrusted with respect to these\nchoices. A request cannot create or replace policy, change its principal,\nregister an executor, grant territory or declare itself owner. Policy bytes\nare acquired and checked again before effects. Their digest checks continuity;\nit does not authenticate whoever wrote them. Authority rests on the trusted\noperator's separately established Product/owner binding.\n\nThe supported deployment is a cooperative local development account: the\noperator and registered executor programs are trusted to honor their declared\noperation contracts. Requests, workspace content and F_P output are untrusted\ninput to the tool. Same-account actors able to rewrite protected policy,\nexecutables or retained evidence behind the server are outside this boundary;\nthe tool provides no OS credential isolation, signing or adversarial concurrent\nfilesystem sandbox. It still detects ordinary dirty state, dependency drift,\nconflicting tool writes, missing evidence and incorrect request boundaries.\nNo internal path is trusted merely because it is internal.\n\nA registered process is **not OS-confined**. Preflight and dispatch enforce\nits exact invocation, input and configuration, check its registered dependency\npreimages, and observe declared effect surfaces. They do not prove that an\narbitrary child cannot write elsewhere or create descendants. An executor's\nqualified contract must honestly declare its tools, local-effect behavior,\ndependency population, termination observations and unobserved host conditions.\nUnsupported enforcement requirements refuse; no `sandboxed` guarantee appears.\n\nPolicy/source roots and the protected evidence root cannot be in any permitted\nWriter territory. All API-relative paths reject absolute paths, `..`, empty or\nambiguous components and symlink components, including a symlink leaf; regular\nfile opens use non-following checks. Immutable Git acquisition resolves an\nexact full object/revision and member, checks regular-blob mode and hash, then\nreads blob bytes without checkout, hooks, filters or a moving branch. Product\nread roots may exceed write territory only where explicitly configured. A\nmissing or inaccessible root is a gap, never permission to search elsewhere.\n\n## Ontology and invariants\n\nThe irreducible domain carriers are the selected policy/binding, exact acquired\ncontent/observations, activated context, one execution attempt, original return\nand downstream operation evidence. Files, CLI messages and MCP results are\nrepresentations of those carriers. No separate mutable task object is needed.\n\n| Carrier | Identity, ownership and relationship |\n|---|---|\n| `OwnerPolicy` | One exact operator-selected id/digest per Runtime, binding one Product definition id/digest and fixed principal. Contains existing grants and approved operation/executor/predicate references. External authority, never public-tool output. |\n| `MethodBinding` | One exact registered profile id/digest and method cut plus member hashes. References owners; maps their packet/result contracts to tenant serialization. |\n| `SourceRef` | One engine, registered root/repository, exact relative path/object and whole-content SHA-256. One optional selector narrows acquisition, never changes parent identity. |\n| `Observation` | One named acquisition scope/time, enumerated path population, existence/mode/byte hashes and relevant configuration/dependency preconditions. Dirty/untracked bytes participate. |\n| `ModelRef` | One exact raw input digest, model id/digest, codec/profile and subject basis; source grounding is separately supplied. Model and carrier identities stay distinct. |\n| `Context` | One caller-selected method packet plus actual record/source payloads, late-acquisition manifest, projection boundaries, rendered stdin bytes and scoped fit evidence. |\n| `Preflight` | One exact activation/context/grant/executor/result-surface tuple, policy and source preimages, finite admission findings and receipt. It does not admit its cited outcome. |\n| `Attempt` | One protected identity/reservation, exact invocation/payload/settings, ordered retained observations, stdout/stderr and named result surface. May have predecessor attempt; never an inferred continuation. |\n| `ClosedReturn` | One original raw payload and producer/activation/subject/basis/consumer bindings, original predicates/domain values, provenance, residuals and invalidators. Checks do not rewrite it. |\n| `OperationEvidence` | One immutable request/response/content manifest and hash-linked observations. Reconstructable downstream evidence, not a work-state authority. |\n| `ExistingCarrier` | An externally owned work/evidence source. Projection does not own its state. Only a named, separately granted Writer operation changes it. |\n\nCross-carrier invariants:\n\n","coordinates":{"lines":[1,120]},"encoding":"utf8","parent_sha256":"faefdf2432759859780d962ca1028f44f7ebca9a5f6a11c324c27ddc258d521f","selected_sha256":"f8a3bd750e9bae0451bd619c6f6ef7bc70005a2f99377a4b58f872cdd16a69ce","size_bytes":8928,"source":{"engine":"workspace-regular-file","object":null,"path":"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-support.md","root":"product","selector":{"lines":[1,120]},"sha256":"faefdf2432759859780d962ca1028f44f7ebca9a5f6a11c324c27ddc258d521f"}}},"schema":"a_c.fd-support.response/1","status":"ok"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01849CXFJcY8KTHUvkyyRQgV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
